{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The hoopoe.</b> This is the wild rooster, whose crest is doubled and whose comb is doubled. And it was the one that brought the shamir to the Temple. So they said in Gittin, chapter 'He who was seized by a deed of Ashmedai': he said to him, 'To me he would not deliver the shamir; to the Prince of the Sea he delivered it, and he gives it only to the wild rooster, whom he trusts with an oath.' And what does he do with it? He brings it to a mountain that has no settlement, sets it on the cleft of the mountain, and the mountain splits; and he takes and brings splinters of wood in his claws and casts them there and kindles them — and that is what we translate (in Targum) נגר טורא (a mountain-carpenter)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:47.698119612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}